The Application event log size must be configured to 32768 KB or greater.
STIG ID: WN11-AU-000500  |  SRG: SRG-OS-000341-GPOS-00132 |  Severity: medium (CAT II)  |  CCI: CCI-001849 |  Vulnerability Id: V-253337

Vulnerability Discussion
Inadequate log size will cause the log to fill up quickly. This may prevent audit events from being recorded properly and require frequent attention by administrative personnel.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

<#
.SYNOPSIS
    Sets the maximum size of the Windows Application event log to 32768 KB (32 MB) or greater, so events are not
    overwritten before they can be collected and reviewed. Windows 11 twin of the course sample WN10-AU-000500.

.NOTES
    Author          : Suad
    LinkedIn        : https://www.linkedin.com/in/suadreskovic/
    GitHub          : https://github.com/suad-dreskovicc
    Date Created    : 2026-11-18
    Last Modified   : 2026-11-18
    Version         : 1.0
    CVEs            : N/A
    Plugin IDs      : N/A (Tenable compliance audit: DISA Microsoft Windows 11 STIG v2r1)
    STIG-ID         : WN11-AU-000500

.TESTED ON
    Date(s) Tested  : 2026-11-18
    Tested By       : Suad Dreskovic
    Systems Tested  : Suad-VM-Test (Windows 11 Pro 25H2, Azure, Cyber Range 1)
    PowerShell Ver. : 5.1

.USAGE
    Run in an elevated (Administrator) PowerShell on the VM:
    PS C:\> .\WN11-AU-000500.ps1
    Then rescan with Tenable ("kk-mde-win11 DISA STIG scan (Win 11)") and confirm WN11-AU-000500 shows Passed.
#>
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# YOUR CODE HERE

$path = 'HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\EventLog\Application'

# The policy key does not exist on a fresh VM, so create it first.
if (-not (Test-Path $path)) { New-Item -Path $path -Force | Out-Null }
New-ItemProperty -Path $path -Name 'MaxSize' -Value 32768 -PropertyType DWord -Force | Out-Null

# Show the result: expect MaxSize = 32768.
Get-ItemProperty -Path $path -Name 'MaxSize' | Select-Object MaxSize

# Remediate Application Event Log Registry Setting

$RegistryPath = "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\EventLog\Application"

# Create registry path if it does not exist
New-Item -Path $RegistryPath -Force | Out-Null

# Set Application Event Log maximum size to 32768 KB
New-ItemProperty -Path $RegistryPath `
    -Name "MaxSize" `
    -PropertyType DWord `
    -Value 32768 `
    -Force | Out-Null

# Verify remediation
Get-ItemProperty -Path $RegistryPath -Name "MaxSize"

Write-Host "Application Event Log remediation completed."
